module contract;

// Monkey `mk_vhost_set` at the release candidate of its va_end fix —
// resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Supplemental card SUP04-VARIADIC-UPSTREAM-CANDIDATES, lock entry by card
// CONTRACT-PIN-TIP-MODE. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream function,
// tracking the TIP of the branch that carries its fix. This module verifies
// nothing: a declaration is a premise, and any verdict that rests on it is a
// verdict RELATIVE TO this declaration. It targets a future, unreleased
// Monkey release (a release candidate), not a released version.
//
// ## The defect and its fix
//
// CG26-VARIADICS (gateway rule 11w) refused `mk_vhost_set` at the pinned
// corpus (`mk_server/mk_lib.c:523`): `va` may reach a function exit without
// `va_end`. The user confirmed the reading in the Monkey repository: the
// `!value` early return inside the `va_arg` loop returned without `va_end`.
// The fix is Monkey commit 21a2c1908b42596317717436e5ce0420805bd523 ("server:
// end variadic arguments on null vhost value"), the tip of branch
// `cosmo0920-missing-va_end-on-null`, which this contract treats as the
// release candidate. Its body, `mk_server/mk_lib.c:509-541` there:
//
//     int mk_vhost_set(mk_ctx_t *ctx, int vid, ...)
//     {
//         ...
//         vh = mk_vhost_lookup(ctx, vid);
//         if (!vh) {
//             return -1;
//         }
//
//         va_start(va, vid);
//
//         while ((key = va_arg(va, char *))) {
//             value = va_arg(va, char *);
//             if (!value) {
//                 /* Wrong parameter */
//                 va_end(va);
//                 return -1;
//             }
//
//             ret = mk_vhost_set_property(vh, key, value);
//             if (ret != 0) {
//                 va_end(va);
//                 return -1;
//             }
//         }
//
//         va_end(va);
//         return 0;
//     }
//
// ## The declaration, clause by clause
//
// * `ctx` and `vid` are borrowed: the body looks the virtual host up and
//   neither releases, stores nor returns `ctx`.
// * The trailing actuals are the NULL-terminated key/value strings. Each
//   value reaches `mk_vhost_set_property`, which copies it (`mk_string_dup`)
//   and reads its length (`strlen`); no trailing pointer is released or
//   retained, so the tail is `resource_variadic_borrowed_tail()` (contract
//   specification C04, cards O04-TRACE and CG26-VARIADICS).
// * The result is a status (0 or -1) that carries no resource.
// * Not stated, because v1 has no words for it: the body changes `ctx`'s
//   interior (a `Name` key appends a newly allocated alias to the virtual
//   host's `server_names`; a `DocumentRoot` key overwrites
//   `documentroot.data` with a fresh copy without releasing an earlier one,
//   read only, not validated). `ctx` stays borrowed: none of this moves
//   custody of a parameter or of a trailing actual.
//
// Read against the fixed body (21a2c190, `mk_server/mk_lib.c:509-541`, with
// `mk_vhost_lookup` at :435 and `mk_vhost_set_property` above it): every
// clause holds on every path, the `!vh` return included (before `va_start`,
// so no `va_list` is live there). No clause changed from the draft.
//
// ## Revision mode: tracking the tip of the fix branch (C06.2, tip identity)
//
// The declaration is pinned (the default, no marker); its entry in this
// crate's `contracts.lock` (format version 3) is a TIP identity, not a
// reviewed revision (the user's decision, 2026-10-02): repository `monkey`
// (https://github.com/cosmo0920/monkey), ref
// `refs/heads/cosmo0920-missing-va_end-on-null`, reviewed at 21a2c190. An
// audit resolves the ref's current commit in the local Monkey repository
// (`QUIRIN_TIP_REPOSITORIES=monkey=PATH`, else the path the lock records),
// requires it to descend from 21a2c190, and keeps this declaration in force
// exactly where the audited source's `mk_vhost_set` sites equal those read
// from that commit's blobs. When the tip moves, it follows the tip: a
// revision no person reviewed, which every run lists as the named assumption
// `tip-tracked:mk_vhost_set` and announces with a notice. It was recorded by
// `quirin-audit pin --source-root <monkey checkout> --crate
// qcore-provider-libevent --function mk_vhost_set --track-tip
// cosmo0920-missing-va_end-on-null --repository-name monkey`.
//
// At the pinned Fluent Bit corpus (66910c10) the vendored copy sits under
// `lib/monkey/` and still has the defect, so the declaration is NOT in force
// there (`source-changed` against the tip, a warning notice); nothing in that
// corpus calls `mk_vhost_set`, and its own body is analysed as an undeclared
// definition either way, so no verdict moves. On a host without the Monkey
// repository the tip is unresolved (`tip-unresolved`), also out of force.
//
// It is not `resource_body_checked` (C06.3): the body is not yet established
// on route G (an unmodelled call in the loop condition, and the uncontracted
// static `mk_vhost_set_property`), so the marker would only withdraw it. The
// va_list protocol itself is decided on the body by rule 11w, independently
// of this declaration.

extern fn mk_vhost_set(ctx: ptr<mut, u8>, vid: i32) -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(ctx);
    ensures normal resource_borrowed(vid);
    ensures normal resource_variadic_borrowed_tail();
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
